				"string" : "## Timeout repair gate investigation — 2026-10-21\nImage-only investigation in SuperGame.image / Pharo13.1.0SNAPSHOT; no source selectors changed and no source publication/build. Successful explicit initial continuity checkpoint retained under current child owner c3a28b26-4597-4d85-938d-285525661537/4zp7vkzl5zf7gu5new36kboda, object 2bw3cop75pbdshmmwe4obxuv3. All five other retained same-parent executions were idle with zero exact execution/chat/provider receiver matches in full suspended sender-chain scans (blocq0y885w573ymcrfjv7soq). This establishes observed provider cessation, not completion of UI work.\nConfirmed source seam: GtLImageDataView>>element: (Gt4LlmCore) implicitly invokes BlScripter>>element:, which synchronously pulses until ready; computedImageBytes evaluates that block during serialization. GtLOpenAiResponsesEndpoint>>serializeToolCall: requests mainDataView serialization. GtLImageDataViewExamples currently cover supplied PNG bytes, not busy-element readiness or cleanup. No controlled rendering reproduction was attempted while the mutation gate remained unresolved.\nRetained diagnosis queue 52iyh9svlkmbh7iggkd56s594 remains under diagnosis owner c3a28b26-4597-4d85-938d-285525661537/d0tth5x9grkl51h8xwf6atotl. Current inspection found zero active and nine pending BlPromiseTasks, all executing/uncomputed and labelled Future: Ollama. Their manual promises originate at AsyncPausableSink>>resume:beforeResuming:. Only one current pausable sink matches these promise identities; each task matches that same current sink promise (di7fnfbvo9qjziu7qunf5ams0). Its buffer is AsyncStreamBuffer id 729; stream loading promise is indefinitely pending, execution pending, worker has no current task/process, group ScrollingList; no task/promise/sink receiver frames found (a524km8jppxpl221hlm5oe88s, eouotbhneynhdn2qmwyjl1wyx, 7h47m2o2l3gjodrq3upkwvvny).\nOwnership traced through buffer -> AsyncMapWithCacheStream -> GtLAsyncExecutionMessageStream -> reply view model. That exact view model is retained by BVCFairyReplyMessageElement and other elements beneath original pane 8wxetod9lg3cq4nbkj46zr9w1; its chat uses BVCFairyProviderStub, is idle, and the reply remains created with no finishedAt (2f1zd5fr0gf8iojv3gx8sei37, bso64r1dsw5715d11ya7vm1qg). This is unfinished example UI, not an identified live Ollama request. AsyncStreamBuffer>>stop delegates cooperative stream termination; it does not itself establish promise completion or remove queued tasks. No stop, promise fulfillment/rejection, queue clearing, process termination, replay or rollback performed.\nGate remains closed: retained UI disposition/actual completion has not been reconciled. Existing partial feedback edits and original exception/diagnosis objects remain untouched and unverified. Next bounded decision: explicitly dispose the identified retained example buffer through existing cooperative stop protocol and verify actual worker/promise/task completion, including the repeated registrations, before modifying GT image serialization. Do not treat waiter timeout or absence of receiver frames as cancellation. No normal/busy/cancellation/resource acceptance checks executed in this investigation."
			},
