					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## Authorized recovery disposition and bounded image repair — 2026-10-21\nSuperGame.image / Pharo13.1.0SNAPSHOT. Successful initial continuity checkpoint recorded. Ownership/rules reread. Exact original pane and buffer 729 re-proven by reply identity through the stream into five original-pane renderers; provider BVCFairyProviderStub (current evidence 2mv495141gkpyxxxrx8wookk0). Only that buffer received AsyncStreamBuffer>>stop. Stream and chunk promises actually became AsyncFulfilledPromiseState, buffer done, worker nil. Nine original registrations all became computed/queued against that same fulfilled chunk promise (4p2kmaj9kro8nrxy1yo1fzmwi). Their sole owning task queue was identified; its existing runOn: protocol drained only those computed BlPromiseTasks, with no promise mutation or queue clearing. Final retained queue count zero, no definite tasks, buffer done (3m0rs0fsf4cbjqw5wrf4f4elt). Six prior exact executions/chats/providers idle with zero receiver matches across full suspended sender chains of 44 nonterminated processes (21usdtkiwxq7trykqi82tgm9y). Recovery gate reconciled; original exceptions and partial feedback edits preserved.\n\nImage-only repair owner: Gt4LlmCore / Gt4LlmCore-Examples, explicit user scope extension, GT/Pharo only. GtLImageDataView>>element: sets existing BlScripter maxPulseElapsedTime: to one second BEFORE attaching/pulsing; ensures target detachment and removal of its added event filter. This is a cooperative readiness limit, not preemption of a blocked pulse/export. computedImageBytes caches the original BlDevScripterPulseTimeoutError in imageReadinessError; repeated failed serialization does not create new scripters. serializeToLlmPrimiteDataOn: returns a supported JSON/text block describing image unavailability, never a fabricated image. Other failures propagate. imageBytes: resets cached bytes/failure. Class-side fromElement: now reuses the same lazy element rendering path rather than its separate default-ten-minute path; sender search found no pre-existing GtLImageDataView consumer for that factory.\n\nChanged selectors: instance element:, computedImageBytes, imageReadinessError, imageBytes:, serializeToLlmPrimiteDataOn:; class fromElement:. Added one failure-evidence slot, no classes/dispatcher/Bloc changes. Examples added: readyElementSerialization, busyElementSerialization, imageComputationFailurePropagates. Current final bounded execution: these three plus two existing supplied-PNG serialization examples passed via direct example invocation, primitive-only report 8zdgxman9aa6ivs0x48eflpw2. Earlier individual GT runner ready/busy passed; initial ready example had a fixture argument error, preserved as d0bayqdhzddpscfuu5exzezmf, corrected before final checks. Busy check asserts under four seconds, text without image, original error identity over three repeats, detached element, and zero remaining fixture tasks in the original temporary space after explicit fixture-owned dequeue. No arbitrary promise settlement used.\n\nLimits: external cancellation acceptance not executed; no hard guarantee against a blocking individual pulse/export, no generic disposal of resources owned by returned elements. No live-provider/end-to-end endpoint or broad regression suite; no feature acceptance of partial feedback implementation; no GemStone validation. Image readiness errors remain inspectable through imageReadinessError, not serialized as images. No source save/export/stage/commit/push/build/external checkout. Remaining next review: cancellation semantics and endpoint integration under bounded fixtures before claiming complete timeout/cancellation acceptance."
			},
