				"string" : "## Ownership/durability review — blocked image slice, 2026-10-21\nOwner sought: CatalystDevKit / BV-Catalyst-Fairy-Core, GT/Pharo only. No source selectors/classes/slots changed by this review. Temporary upstream GtLImageDataView patch and its three examples remain exactly as found; not restored without a verified replacement and exact original baseline. Partial Barry activity/UI work preserved. No save/export/commit/push/build/startup patch or external checkout.\n\nCurrent child owner c3a28b26-4597-4d85-938d-285525661537/a2k6gt1a3l5n94269l4nptrhd. Successful explicit continuity checkpoint and self identification: 6wh6l37o44uk04qgy383vm6fx. Seven prior same-parent executions idle, zero exact execution/chat/provider receiver matches in full sender-chain scans over 44 nonterminated processes: 3t8d9jb20wji08h6i993z6exa. Prior repair child 6s3xmg2ma4k9n9nno75rog1x1 retained reconciliation re-read: its 3m0rs0fsf4cbjqw5wrf4f4elt = zero retained queue tasks/no definite tasks/buffer done; its 21usdtkiwxq7trykqi82tgm9y retains fulfilled stream/chunk promises and nil worker. This review did not repeat stop/drain or mutate promises.\n\nSelection gap: GtLWrappedModel>>computeMainDataView creates GtLDataView new; ProtoObject collection enters GtLDataViewsCollector, whose collect creates GtLDataView empty for each pragma. GtLDataView>>imageData directly constructs GtLImageDataView. Forwarded object views recursively enter the same generic builder. GtLDataViewContext is empty and carries no image factory/policy. Merely subclassing a root data view does not reach those nested images. No supported per-chat recursive builder/image selection hook was demonstrated. Existing model userMessageEndpoint: is a real endpoint-selection seam; however an endpoint-local solution still needs a supported recursive image transformation/factory contract while preserving keys, labels, provenance, caching and text evidence. It has not been implemented or integration-tested. BVCFairyCodexClient handles HTTP lifecycle after serialization, not image construction; no transport workaround added.\n\nRestoration blocker: registered IceRepository lookup for GtLImageDataView package returned nil. Registry contains Catalyst repositories but not Gt4LlmCore's owner. No unregistered checkout discovery performed. Retained prior tool-call history confirms the six changed selectors (instance element:, computedImageBytes, imageBytes:, serializeToLlmPrimiteDataOn:, imageReadinessError; class fromElement:), added imageReadinessError slot and three added examples readyElementSerialization/busyElementSerialization/imageComputationFailurePropagates. Exact original method/class definitions were not recovered against an owning repository baseline in this slice; no guessed rollback.\n\nFocused current execution on SuperGame.image / Pharo13.1.0SNAPSHOT: five existing examples invoked directly, all passed, primitive report 8pawsbm5c1wox1oif16jhrqh9. Includes ready/busy image, cached error/repeats/cleanup, unrelated computation error and two supplied-PNG serialization checks. These validate the temporary patch only, NOT Catalyst ownership or endpoint integration. No broad suite/live model/network/default-ten-minute pulse. External cancel, single blocking pulse/export preemption, generic GT restoration and rebuild persistence remain unverified; actual maintained Barry-local path is unmet.\n\nCandidate upstream dependency: provide a recursively propagated data-view/image factory or serialization policy selected per tool execution/chat, defaulting to current generic GT behavior; retain original readiness error with bounded cooperative rendering and cleanup. Verify normal/busy/repeat/unrelated errors through the real endpoint, then select it only for Barry via existing model endpoint/consumer seam and restore only the exact temporary patch against an exposed original baseline. This is a proposal, not an implemented capability or authority expansion. Separately authorized supported source publication followed by a BVC rebuild remains necessary for rebuild delivery; current temporary changes are image-only."
			},
