				"string" : "## Barry-local progress and gate diagnosis — 2026-10-22\nOwner CatalystDevKit / BV-Catalyst-Fairy-Core; SuperGame.image / Pharo13.1.0SNAPSHOT. This supersedes the historical blocked next-action guidance above, not historical outcomes. Initial checkpoint succeeded (7oml56opcufuimfdn1izskh71). Current child 58faemel1jbi9ubt9ncmvi6qf retained. Affirmative current ownership investigation: both preceding exact executions idle, no pending Barry UI; full suspended sender-chain scan across 44 nonterminated processes found no execution/chat/provider receiver matches for either predecessor, and one for this running child (1puv38lvkrr9blfj77wc35q3i). No stop/reset/replay/termination/rollback performed; no claim that missing older objects prove cessation.\n\nRoot cause: production unfinishedMaintainerFor: already checks current provider state and registered Barry UI ownership, NOT historical lifecycle records. Prior no-progress diagnosis incorrectly promoted inaccessible historical evidence into an eternal mutation prerequisite. Separately, Maintainer examples using the production global registry collided with this genuinely active child. Do not weaken the live gate to make examples pass. Factored hasLiveMutationOwnership and mutationOwnershipRootsFor:, preserved production registered-chat scope, and added a test-only builder stub with isolated roots. Gate diagnostics now name execution id, current provider state and pending UI instead of inaccurately saying every conflict is 'still stopping'. mutationOwnershipStatus is an inspectable query. Running/stopping/non-idle and outstanding Barry UI still block; unavailable inspection never clears ownership; idle ownership does not rewrite unknown history or prove task acceptance. Arbitrary external UI/resource ownership still needs specific investigation when identified, not an inference from an empty scan.\n\nImage increment is deliberately narrower than timed rendering: BVCFairyResponsesEndpoint subclasses the existing Codex Responses endpoint and is selected only by BVCFairyChat>>installCodexClientFor:. It traverses existing composite/forwarded targets at serialization, preserving their caches, keys, native builder and provenance. Supplied ByteArray or already cached image bytes become input_image blocks alongside the original JSON text. Deferred computations are NEVER invoked: explicit imageStatus unavailable/reason text replaces that image. Thus no scripter, readiness wait, retry worker, failure cache or cleanup resource is created by this policy. Existing image cache is reused, not mutated. No lazy render timeout/cancellation/preemption guarantee is claimed; no new renderer exists. Label computations and non-image native views retain native error behavior. Documents retain the existing tool endpoint behavior. Barry Codex roots/children select this path; ordinary GT chats unchanged. Private GT slot names computedImageBytes/imageBytesComputation are a known compatibility dependency, confined to this consumer, not GT extensions. No live network/provider acceptance check. Other provider endpoints and user-message attachment rendering are outside this increment.\n\nChanged production selectors: BVCFairyAgentExecution>>hasLiveMutationOwnership, mutationOwnershipStatus; BVCFairyAgentBuilder>>mutationOwnershipRootsFor:, unfinishedMaintainerFor:, validateForParent:ifErrorDo:; BVCFairyChat>>installCodexClientFor:; new BVCFairyResponsesEndpoint>>serializeDataView:on:, primitiveDataFor:, serializeToolCall:. New example classes BVCFairyImageExamples (six examples plus fixture) and BVCFairyAgentBuilderStub (roots:, mutationOwnershipRootsFor:). Recovery examples changed blockedMaintainerStillAllowsInspection, freshChatCannotBypassConflictingMaintainer, runningUiWorkKeepsMutationGateClosed, cancellationAbandonsQueuedUiWork; added idleOwnershipDoesNotRewriteUnknownHistory and unavailableObservationDoesNotChangeGate. Continuity initialCheckpointFailureBlocksWork and timeoutPreservesResultAndBlocksOverlappingMaintainer now use the isolated builder; latter ensures fixture idle cleanup. Fairy emptyToolsUseRoleDefaults tests role construction without starting a competing live Maintainer. Existing actual tool-call examples still cover delegation.\n\nVerification: final existing GT example runner, eight classes (Image, Recovery, Continuity, Fairy, Codex, Activity, ChatElement, WindowTitle): 98 successes, zero failures/errors/skips. Earlier runs and errors retained, not concealed. Original role-default failure and two continuity gate errors were current-active-child fixture collisions, not permission to bypass the production gate. New checks cover ready supplied/cached bytes, deferred failure-producing block never called over repeats, nested forwarded mixed image content, actual endpoint tool output and Barry-only root/child selection. Retained endpoint output 90v1umnw595w4kcrv0jocbklu; nested primitive data 6821m2msh4cgth9olh9pi3k0v; live UI ownership test d9mnf4voxvgtd9tj18km82saj. Previous reported 118 checks are historical and not the count of this selected run. No GemStone/native platform claims, rebuild, interactive UX acceptance, live provider/network or broad upstream suite.\n\nPending image source changes only. No upstream GT class/method/slot/extension edits, Foundation/Runtime changes, source save/export/stage/commit/push/build or external checkout. Current loaded GtLImageDataView>>element: was generic on inspection (historical temporary patch is not a prerequisite or a change made here). Remaining acceptance gap: bounded actual lazy rendering is not implemented; this increment safely delivers ready images and explicit unavailable evidence without rendering. A future rendering requirement must choose a Barry-owned construction contract rather than silently reintroducing generic ten-minute pulsing."
			}
		]
	},
